# ModDB Release Archive Structure

When creating a release archive for `hodvisualizer`, the zip must be ModDB-compatible.

## Required archive layout

- `modinfo.json` must exist at the **root** of the `.zip`.
- `HodVisualizer.dll`, `HodVisualizer.deps.json`, and `assets/...` must be at root-level paths (not nested under `hodvisualizer/`).

## Packaging rule

- Do **not** zip the parent folder (`hodvisualizer/`) itself.
- Zip `bin/Release/Mods/hodvisualizer/*` so files land directly in archive root.

## Mandatory verification before handing archive to user

Run a quick archive entry check and confirm root `modinfo.json` exists.

Example verification command:

`Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem; $z=[System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::OpenRead("<zipPath>"); $z.Entries | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName }; $z.Dispose()`

## Stop condition

If `modinfo.json` is not in archive root, rebuild archive before reporting success.
